{"name":"Nautilus","hex":"#273c5a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nautilus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marine mollusc, of the family Nautilidae native to the Pacific Ocean and Indian Ocean, which has tentacles and a spiral shell with a series of air-filled chambers, of which Nautilus is the type genus.","A kind of diving bell that sinks or rises by means of compressed air."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nautilus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nautilus","blocks":[{"text":"A nautilus is any of the various species within the cephalopod family Nautilidae. This is the sole extant family of the superfamily Nautilaceae, suborder Nautilina, order Nautilida, and subclass Nautiloidea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Nautilus_belauensis_from_Palau.jpg/330px-Nautilus_belauensis_from_Palau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nautilus","wikidata":"Q223939"},{"title":"Nautilus (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Nautilus is a ten-part adventure drama television series created by James Dormer. It is a reimagining of the 1870 novel Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas by Jules Verne, presenting an origin story for Captain Nemo, an Indian prince-turned-crusading scientist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a6/Nautilus_%282024%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nautilus_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q111169891"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/The_first_and_oldest_fossil_of_Chambered_Nautilus_displayed_at_Philippine_National_Museum.jpg/500px-The_first_and_oldest_fossil_of_Chambered_Nautilus_displayed_at_Philippine_National_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Th